  "body": "## What happens\n\nRotary Contour refuses a cylindrical workpiece whose axis is X.\nThis prevents the A-axis catalog case in #2869.\n\nAt upstream/main `58cb641ca`, `crates/motion/src/multiaxis/rotary.rs:76` defines `rotary_contour`.\nIt computes `abs(axis.dir.dot(UP))`.\nFor an X axis, this value is zero.\nThe guard below `0.0175` returns this diagnostic:\n\n```\nthe work's axis lies flat on the table - a laid bar is finished with passes along it: Rotary Parallel\n```\n\nThe existing test `the_kinds_refuse_each_other_degenerate_stances_by_name` requires this refusal for `laid_bar(16)`.\nSee `crates/motion/tests/rotary.rs:320`.\n\n## Expected result\n\nRotary Contour can cut rings around a cylindrical workpiece on A about X.\nRotary Parallel is a workaround for finishing, but it does not show contour rings.\n\nThe current station conversion divides by the axis Z component.\nRemoving the guard alone is not a fix.\nThe fix must define the station heights and keep the clearance and gouge checks.\n\n## Related work\n\n- #2774 changes rotary heights to radii.\n- #2772 adds a stated rotary axis for freeform workpieces.\n- #2869 needs this behavior for a catalog example.\n- #2392 tracks the example catalog.\n\nDone means: A cylindrical workpiece along X generates Rotary Contour rings, passes verification, and posts finite A-axis moves.\nTests must measure the rings and the clearance, and reject unsafe input by name.\n",
